Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?rl-patches(engine):=20npc=20render=20distance?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20dormant=20npcs=20outside=20RL=5FNPC=5FRADIUS?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An idle world spent 2.03 ms of a 2.88 ms cycle (71%) calling npc.turn() on
7,321 static npcs, of which an agent inside its 52-tile scan can see roughly 50.
Every world process paid it, so it set the ceiling on tick rate and therefore on
honest throughput.

processNpcs() now builds the set of 64x64 chunks holding a player, dilated by
RL_NPC_RADIUS tiles (default 64, must stay >= the agent's 52-tile npc scan), and
gives every npc outside it Npc.dormantTurn() instead of Npc.turn(). dormantTurn
runs the respawn/revert/despawn countdown ONLY, so an npc killed before the agent
walked away still comes back; everything whose effect nobody can observe (hunt,
regen, timers, queues, movement, facing) is skipped. Set RL_NPC_RADIUS=0 for
vanilla behaviour.

Measured, one world, 24 agents, CHOP, A/B on the same build:
  gate off  fastest honest 5ms -> 199.2 t/s, 1617 dec/s
  gate on   fastest honest 3ms -> 325.5 t/s, 2607 dec/s   (4ms: 249.7 t/s, 2395)
Machine-wide honest best moves from the recorded 1,075 dec/s (2 worlds x 12 @ 8ms)
to 4,709 dec/s (3 worlds x 24 @ 5ms, 98.9% of asked).
